    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0546" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Netherlands/52: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Emmet</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-07T15:00:00-05:00">December 7, 1935—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Your No. 88, December 5, 1 p.m. Make formal request as stated in second
                    paragraph, adding that former smuggling bases have gradually been closed and
                    smugglers now compelled to obtain cargoes alcohol in European ports and
                    discharge them on high seas into smuggling vessels; that in order to circumvent
                    this latest move of smugglers and prevent them from getting foothold in
                    Netherlands, we believe it would be mutually desirable if Netherland Government
                    would take action requested, or promise to do so in future if smugglers transfer
                    their operations to Dutch territory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
